./design/sources/platform/chat.pen:240246:      "content": "Why does a user see the 'Archived' badge?\n\nWhen a user archives a conversation, it disappears from the sidebar to reduce clutter. However, if they later search for it, the conversation still appears in results. The 'Archived' badge tells the user this conversation is no longer in their active sidebar — so they understand why they can't find it there. Clicking the result should still open the conversation normally."
./design/sources/platform/chat.pen:240256:      "content": "Archived chat state: When a user opens an archived conversation (e.g. from search results), the chat input is replaced with an archived banner showing an archive icon, 'This conversation was archived' text, and an 'Unarchive' button. The conversation content remains fully readable. Clicking 'Unarchive' restores the chat input and returns the conversation to the sidebar."
