./docs/en/develop/webdav-api.md:149:The endpoint advertises `DAV: 1, 2`. Treat the methods and limitations on this page as the implementation contract; the advertisement is not a promise that every optional WebDAV feature works. In particular, dead properties do not persist and shared editing locks are not available. Calendar, contact, search, and ACL extensions are not provided.
./docs/en/develop/webdav-api.md:183:Use [REST](/develop/api-reference) for project-scoped imports, explicit IDs, and search. Use WebDAV for Document Hub file clients that expect paths and locks. Both work with Tale documents, but WebDAV does not expose the project's file tree or every REST operation.
